---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About VatSnap — Free, Unofficial EU VAT Tool"
  description="VatSnap is a free, unofficial EU VAT rate calculator for small online sellers. Rates come from the open-source eu-vat-rates-data package (EU TEDB source)."
  canonicalPath="/about/"
>
  <h1>About VatSnap</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    VatSnap is a free, unofficial VAT rate calculator built for small online
    sellers — Etsy, Shopify, Amazon and independent shops selling into the EU.
  </p>
  <div class="card">
    <h2>Where the numbers come from</h2>
    <p>
      Every rate on this site is bundled at build time from the open-source
      <code>eu-vat-rates-data</code> npm package, which tracks the European
      Commission's Taxes in Europe Database (TEDB). No rate is ever typed by
      hand into the UI — the calculator reads the dataset directly, so updates
      to the package flow straight through on the next build.
    </p>
    <h2>Important disclaimer</h2>
    <p>
      VatSnap is a guidance tool, not tax advice. VAT treatment depends on
      place of supply, customer status, product category, thresholds and
      exemptions that this calculator cannot know. Always confirm rates and
      filing obligations with a qualified accountant or the official EU TEDB
      source before invoicing or filing.
    </p>
    <h2>Cost &amp; privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The site is fully static — no backend, no database, no accounts, no
      tracking. Calculations happen in your browser, and hosting on Cloudflare
      Pages costs $0.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
